Origins
-------

The router firmware (Mk2_1phase_RFdatalog_temp) derives from the 3-phase router firmware
of the same author, Mk2_3phase_RFdatalog_temp of PVRouter-3-phase (GPL-3.0-or-later),
itself derived from Robin Emley's 3-phase Mk2 PV Router sketch. Its control core, which
predicts the energy of each mains cycle and decides once per cycle, is that of Robin
Emley's single-phase sketch Mk2_fasterControl_twoLoads_5.ino (July 2023), whose multi-load
logic comes from his Mk2_multiLoad_wired_7a.ino (not in this repository), as ported in
Mk2_fasterControl_Full; its displays come from Mk2_fasterControl_Full as well.

The older sketches are kept as they are, for reference:

- Robin/ holds two of his single-phase sketches, Mk2_fasterControl_twoLoads_5 and
  Mk2_fasterControl_RFdatalog_1.
- Mk2_fasterControl_Full, Mk2_fasterControl_twoLoads_temp_1 and
  Mk2_fasterControl_threeLoads_temp_1 are Frédéric Metrich's versions of his
  fasterControl sketches.
- dev/ holds his test and calibration tools: RST_104us_dev, RST_375us_dev,
  RawSamplesTool_2chan, Transformer_Checker, balanceCheck_1kW, blink_dig4,
  cal_CT1_v_meter, cal_CT2_v_CT1, cal_bothDisplays_3 and segCheck_bothDisplays.

He published his sketches on the OpenEnergyMonitor forum (summary page:
www.openenergymonitor.org/emon/node/1757) and on www.mk2pvrouter.co.uk, for others to
build PV routers with, without any license statement. His sketches in Robin/ and dev/ are
kept as he published them and carry no license tag.

The changes made since 2020 are by Frédéric Metrich and the contributors listed on
GitHub, under GPL-3.0-or-later.


Your settings
-------------

The files that hold your settings are yours: use, change and share them on any terms you
like. These are, for the router, config.h, config_system.h, config_rf.h and calibration.h
(and the config.h, config_system.h and calibration.h of Mk2_fasterControl_Full), whether
you edit them by hand or a tool writes them. They carry no license tag for that reason.


